 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "You live in a dry village in Rajasthan, India. It rains hard for two months, then almost nothing.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "When the storms come, the water races off the bare hills and is gone in a day.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "By spring, every well in the village is dry.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you pile up a low wall of dirt across the dry stream. A curved one, like a smile.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Next storm, the water stops behind it and makes a pond. Problem solved!",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But by winter, the pond is empty again.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Here's the trick. It didn't just dry up. Most of it soaked into the ground.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Down there, it fills the cracks in the rock, and the wells downhill come back to life.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then a monster storm hits. The pond rises, and spills over the top.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Water running over dirt eats it fast, and your wall washes out.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you rebuild it, and give it a stone spillway at one end, so extra water leaves safely.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And rocks on the slope, so the waves can't chew it.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Now one village builds one. The next village builds ten.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Since 1985, people in Rajasthan have built thousands of them, mostly by hand.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And in the 1990s, the Arvari River, dry for years, started flowing all year again.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built a dam that refills the ground. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
